<title>UK: Paris Club cuts and reschedules Benin's debt.</title>
<headline>Paris Club cuts and reschedules Benin's debt.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris Club of creditor nations has cut the debt of the West African state of Benin by 67 per cent, Radio France Internationale reported.</p>
<p>The radio, monitored by the British Broadcasting Corporation on Tuesday, said the remaining debt was rescheduled over 23 years, with a six-year grace period.</p>
<p>The radio said this was the fourteenth rescheduling of Benin's debt since 1989. It did not say how much was involved this time.</p>
</text>
